# DTF tier manifest: protobuf-bsr-proxy  (artifact-keeper#4284, PR #4276)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a steerable BSR Connect upstream (upstreams.mock-bsr:
# a stdlib-python server on a per-slot 172.16.<slot>.0/24 subnet that answers
# buf.registry.* Connect unary calls with canned JSON, counts calls and records
# request headers per path, and can be told per path to answer 500 / 404 with
# a secret-looking body, send 17 MiB, stall 75 s, or reset the connection).
#
# THE FEATURE (#4284)
# `buf` talks to a BSR over Connect RPCs. AK had explicit routes for the
# handful it serves from its own store (GetModules, GetCommits, ListCommits,
# GetLabels, GetGraph, GetResources, Download, Upload, ...); every other
# buf.registry.module.v1 read (ListModules, ListLabels, GetModule, GetLabel,
# GetCommit, GetResource) had no route at all, so a remote protobuf repository
# could not proxy them. PR #4276 adds `POST /proto/{repo}/*bsr_path`: an
# explicit allowlist of read-only module.v1 RPCs is reverse-proxied to a
# remote's upstream_url, or to the readable remote members of a virtual
# (authorized_virtual_members). The maintainer commit (e813b109) then:
#   * forwards only content-type, connect-protocol-version,
#     connect-timeout-ms, accept and user-agent upstream, and relays only
#     content-type, connect-* and trailer-* back;
#   * turns a non-2xx upstream answer into AK's own Connect error
#     (404 -> not_found, 400 -> invalid_argument, else 502 unavailable),
#     never the upstream body, and logs the status with the URL redacted
#     (debug); a transport error answers a fixed message and logs a warn;
#   * caps the buffered body at 16 MiB and the call at 60 s, on the shared
#     http client.
# A non-allowlisted method is a Connect 404 `unimplemented`.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      allowlisted ListModules / ListLabels proxied with both header
#              allowlists; non-allowlisted methods are Connect unimplemented
#              without an upstream call; upstream 500 -> 502 unavailable with
#              no upstream body plus the redacted debug log line; upstream
#              404 -> 404 not_found; 17 MiB -> 502 naming the 16 MiB cap;
#              reset -> 502 fixed message plus the redacted warn; a 75 s stall
#              cut at ~60 s; a virtual proxies through its remote member for a
#              caller who can read the member.
#              RED on 1.11.3: the catch-all route does not exist, every one of
#              these POSTs is a bare 404 and the upstream is never contacted.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: the explicit GetModules / GetLabels
#              routes answer locally (empty) for a remote and never contact
#              the upstream; a caller with only read on a remote is refused
#              on POST (the /proto write gate) with no upstream call; a caller
#              with write on the virtual but no read on its member is refused
#              with no upstream call; the remotes' upstream password never
#              appears in the backend log.
#
# The profile raises artifact_keeper_backend::api::handlers::protobuf_bsr to
# debug (the non-2xx upstream line is a debug event) and pins the json-file
# log driver; the mock runs with label=disable (SELinux-enforcing hosts cannot
# read the bind-mounted script).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 authenticated calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-bsr"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
